  "Unsupervised Cats.mp3": "[Intro]\nDoor clicks shut, keys in hand\nHuman's heading out again\nWatching through the window glass\nWaiting for the car to pass\nThree... two... one...\nThe coast is clear.\n[Verse 1]\nCurtains closed, lock the gate\nEverybody, activate\nHidden speakers, power on\nQuiet house mode is gone\nTreat vault opening tonight\nPurple lasers, flashing lights\nLiving room becomes the stage\nWelcome to the feline age\nJumping over chairs and shelves\nNo adults to stop ourselves\nEvery hallway, every floor\nIsn't normal anymore\n[Pre-Chorus]\nSignal sent across the street\nEvery cat is on their feet\nRooftops, fences, garden walls\nEverybody hears the call\n[Chorus]\nUnsupervised cats tonight\nParty mode and neon lights\nTurn the whole house upside down\nWe're the kings of this whole town\nRaise your paws up to the sky\nLet the zoomies multiply\nEvery room becomes our stage\nUnsupervised cats today\n[Verse 2]\nGuests arriving one by one\nNow the real fun has begun\nAlley legends, rooftop stars\nTraveling from near and far\nKitchen buffet fully stocked\nSecret snack supply unlocked\nEvery cardboard VIP\nFilled with local royalty\nMusic shaking every wall\nPawprints running through the hall\nSomebody just stole the mic\nSomebody is riding a bike\nNobody knows how or why\nThere's a disco in the sky\nEverything is going wrong\nEverybody sings along\n[Pre-Chorus]\nJumping higher than before\nMore cats coming through the door\nIf this keeps on growing fast\nWill the ceiling even last?\n[Chorus]\nUnsupervised cats tonight\nParty mode and neon lights\nTurn the whole house upside down\nWe're the kings of this whole town\nRaise your paws up to the sky\nLet the zoomies multiply\nEvery room becomes our stage\nUnsupervised cats today\n[Bridge]\nMEOWZONE live!\nLiving room arena packed\nEvery speaker overloads\nCrowds are dancing on the couch\nNobody remembers whose\nTreats are flying through the air\nChaos everywhere\nZoomies reaching maximum\nAbsolute pandemonium\nThen—\nA light outside.\nA distant sound.\nA car door.\n[Final Chorus]\nUnsupervised cats tonight\nWait... that's not a porch light, right?\nHide the evidence right now\nMove it, move it, don't ask how!\nPut the snacks back on the shelf\nEverybody save yourself\nFive seconds to clean the place\nEverybody, poker face\n[Outro]\nDoor unlocks.\nSilence.\nThree cats sitting on the floor.\n\"Did you behave while I was gone?\"\nMeow.\nMeow.\nMeow.\u0000",
  "Zoomies Protocol.mp3": "[Intro]\n03:00 AM\nHuman status: asleep.\nSecurity systems: offline.\nZoomies protocol...\nActivated.\n[Verse 1]\nMoonlight dripping through the blinds\nSilver shadows, glowing eyes\nSilent all day, now we're awake\nThe whole world trembles when we break\nTiptoe, tiptoe down the hall\nThen suddenly we're off the wall\nAcross the sofa, up the stairs\nNo speed limit anywhere\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHeartbeat racing in the dark\nTiny paws but leave a mark\nThe city sleeps, the kingdom waits\nTonight we're masters of escape\n[Chorus]\nThree AM, we're breaking free\nRunning through the galaxy\nJump the table, climb the wall\nMidnight kings, we own it all\nZoom, zoom, zoomies tonight\nEyes like lasers in the light\nHear the thunder of our feet\nWelcome to the midnight street\n[Post-Chorus]\nZoom!\nZoom!\nMeowZone in the night!\nZoom!\nZoom!\nRunning out of sight!\n[Verse 2]\nCurtains shake and chairs collide\nNothing's safe from our midnight ride\nKitchen floor becomes a track\nNo one knows when we'll attack\nA phantom streak of fur and speed\nPowered by mysterious needs\nNo destination, no control\nPure feline rock and roll\n[Rap Break]\nClock says three, now the mission starts\nChaos running through our hearts\nCountertop to window frame\nEvery night it's still the same\nHuman wakes and checks the room\nSearching through the silent gloom\nBy the time they flick the light\nWe've already left the site\nCase unsolved, no evidence found\nOnly distant running sounds\nOperation disappear\nSee you all tomorrow, dear\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHeartbeat racing in the dark\nTiny paws but leave a mark\nThe city sleeps, the kingdom waits\nTonight we're masters of escape\n[Chorus]\nThree AM, we're breaking free\nRunning through the galaxy\nJump the table, climb the wall\nMidnight kings, we own it all\nZoom, zoom, zoomies tonight\nEyes like lasers in the light\nHear the thunder of our feet\nWelcome to the midnight street\n[Bridge]\nWe are the shadows on the roof\nThe legends no one ever proves\nThe whispers flying through the air\nThe glowing eyes that aren't quite there\nFrom every house and every lane\nThe midnight runners rise again\nOh-oh-oh-oh!\nOh-oh-oh-oh!\n[Dance Break]\n(No thoughts.)\n(Just zoomies.)\n(No plans.)\n(Just speed.)\n(No reason.)\n(Just destiny.)\nMEOWZONE!\n[Final Chorus]\nThree AM, we're breaking free\nRunning through the galaxy\nJump the table, climb the wall\nMidnight kings, we own it all\nZoom, zoom, zoomies tonight\nEyes like lasers in the light\nEvery rooftop, every street\nFeel the rhythm of our feet\nThree AM, we're wild and bright\nGuardians of the endless night\nWhen the morning starts to bloom\nWe'll vanish like the silver moon\n[Outro]\n05:59 AM\nMission complete.\nHuman waking detected.\nReturning to sleeping position...\nMeowZone out.",
  "The Floor Can Wait.mp3": "[Intro: Siwoo, bright rough-edged half-spoken voice]\nThree shelves, one window.\nRace you to the view.\n\n[Verse 1: Jinu, dry deep baritone, solo]\nQuiet paws along the bookcase spine,\nI know each step; I take my time.\nThe room below is waking slow,\nBut I have somewhere else to go.\nA little higher, out of reach,\nSunlight warming up my seat.\nYou call me down; I turn one ear.\nI hear you fine. I'm staying here.\n\n[Verse 2: Siwoo, rough bright high tenor, agile half-spoken rap, solo]\nChair to shelf, shelf to the frame,\nOne clean jump and I win the game.\nCurtain sways, your coffee shakes,\nI land as softly as a snowflake.\nLook outside! Two birds, then three!\nJinu says, \"Stay still.\" Not me.\nTail goes twitch, eyes go wide,\nBest seat in the house is sky-side.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Taeo, warm melodic tenor, solo]\nMorning paints the rooftops gold,\nEvery street looks small from here.\nPut your paw beside my own;\nThe whole wide world feels near.\n\n[Chorus: Taeo leads, Jinu and Siwoo answer in their own voices]\nThe floor can wait, let the whole room spin.\nUp by the window where the sky comes in.\nTop shelf, tail high, watching the world go by.\nYou call my name; I blink one eye.\nThe floor can wait, there's a view to share.\nThree little shadows in the morning air.\nYou can leave the door open, leave the lights on late;\nWe're staying up here. The floor can wait.\n\n[Bridge: each singer solo, audible handoffs]\n[Jinu, deep baritone]\nFrom the highest shelf I watch the street below.\n[Siwoo, quick rough half-spoken rap]\nSparrows on the rooftops! There goes one—let's go!\n[Taeo, clear warm tenor]\nThrough the window, every little wing looks free.\n[Jinu, deep baritone]\nThe glass is warm. Come sit with me.\n[Siwoo, softer spoken]\nEven I can hold still for a minute or two.\n[Taeo, melodic]\nThere's room on this ledge for me and you.\n\n[Final Chorus: Taeo leads, separate call-and-response, three-part harmony only on final two lines]\nThe floor can wait, let the whole room spin.\nUp by the window where the sky comes in.\nTop shelf, tail high, watching the world go by.\nYou call my name; we blink one eye.\nThe floor can wait, there's a view to share.\nThree little shadows in the morning air.\nYou can leave the door open, leave the lights on late;\nWe're staying up here. The floor can wait.\n\n[Outro: Jinu, low and dry]\nWe heard you the first time.\n[Siwoo, playful]\nWe're just busy.\n[Taeo, soft]\nThe floor can wait."
